<title>JAPAN: TSE SAYS SEEKS TO LIST I-NET CORP.</title>
<headline>TSE SAYS SEEKS TO LIST I-NET CORP.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tokyo Stock Exchange (TSE) said on Tuesday it had applied to the Finance Ministry to list I-Net Corp.</p>
<p>The company is likely to be listed on the second section of the TSE on September 18, the TSE said.</p>
<p>The company plans to issue 500,000 new shares and offer 250,000 through a secondary offering, the TSE said.</p>
<p>I-Net, which is now traded on the over-the-counter (OTC) market, offers information services and develops software.</p>
